[{:db/id 17592186344229 :question/problem "The triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nis defined over the type I region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2},\\,-2\\le y\\le 4,\\,0\\le z\\le 1+xy}.\n$$\n\nUse $[a,b]$ as the full nonempty projection of the exactly specified region $R$ onto the $y$ axis. The inner limits may be piecewise. What is $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "The inequalities defining $R$ are retained exactly. For every $y\\in[-2,4]$, choosing $x=0$ leaves the nonempty fiber $0\\le z\\le1$. Thus the full nonempty $y$ projection is $[a,b]=[-2,4]$ and $a+b=2$.\n\nThe base must also satisfy $1+xy\\ge0$. When $y<0$, this requires $x\\le-1/y$. The bounds $y^2$ and $-1/y$ meet at $y=-1$. Hence\n\n$$\\iiint_R f\\,dV=\\int_{-2}^{-1}\\int_0^{-1/y}\\int_0^{1+xy}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy+\\int_{-1}^4\\int_0^{y^2}\\int_0^{1+xy}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy.$$\n\nOn the first branch the $x$ cap is $-1/y$; on the second it is $y^2$. The source solution used $x\\le y^2$ throughout and therefore included reversed $z$ bounds for some negative $y$. Its isolated expression $1+xz$ is also a transcription error: the upper $z$ bound is $1+xy$. These solution errors do not change the correct endpoint sum $2$." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
